<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4957" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀμάριος</span></b> , fem. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀμαρία</span></b> , epith. of Zeus and Athena in Achaea, <i><span class="en">
			<u>SIG</u>
			490
		</span></i> (Orchomenus in Arcadia, <span class="entity">iii B. C.</span>), cf. <i><span class="en">
			<u>Sammelb.</u>
			357
		</span></i> (<span class="entity">Egypt</span>): —<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀμάριον</span></b> , τό,
		precinct at Aegium in which the Achaean League met, prob. l. in <i><span class="en">
			Str.
			8.7.3
		</span></i> and <i><span class="en">
			5
		</span></i> (but <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὁμάριον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					5.93.10
				</span></i>
			, hence <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀμάριος</span> prob. 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὁμάριος, Ὁμαγύριος</span>
			 (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμαρεῖν, ἁμαρτῆ</span>), and
			is not connected with <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμάρα</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡμέρα</span>
			).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
</div>